# Commit messages

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) aligned with this repo's history.

## Format

```
type: short subject in imperative mood

Required body: short bullet points explaining implementation.
```

- **Subject:** imperative ("add", not "added"); ~72 characters or fewer
- **Body:** focus on purpose and impact; complete sentences

## Types

| Type       | Use for                                   |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| `feat`     | New user-facing behavior                  |
| `fix`      | Bug fixes                                 |
| `chore`    | Tooling, deps, config (no feature change) |
| `docs`     | README or comments only                   |
| `refactor` | Code change without behavior change       |

## Examples (this repo)

```
feat: add in-browser Whisper Tiny transcription with background preload

Integrate Transformers.js in a Web Worker with model preload on page load.
```

```
feat: add client-side MP3 upload UI with validation
```

## Safety

- **Never commit** `.env`, `.env.local`, or any file containing API keys or secrets
- **Only create commits** when the user explicitly asks
- Do not push unless the user explicitly asks
- Match tone and structure of `git log` on this branch

## Do not

- Vague subjects: "update", "fix stuff", "WIP"
- Subject lines that end with a period
- Bodies that only list filenames without explaining why
